# Production parts for the multi-object 3MF plate deliverable,
# build/ovodyo-plate.3mf (scripts/plate.sh, gate.sh --check). The parts print
# SEPARATELY and assemble by hand, so the deliverable is the plate (N distinct
# objects the slicer imports as N parts), never the assembled render, which
# would import as one welded body (the multi-part-fuse rule).
#
# One line per part VALUE (plate.sh merges each ci.parts value once): a part
# printed more than once — base-end (two wings) and base-plug (one per ballast
# pocket) — is listed once here and duplicated in the slicer; the README says
# how many of each. Coupons, fit-check parts (core-seat*, pocket-*), the
# preview-only mock-drive sample and the assembled preview are NOT plate parts.
hours-top
hours-bottom
minutes-top
minutes-bottom
base-segment
base-end
base-core
base-plug
